					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: ANIMATING TEXT\n\nIn this example we take a string and find how long it is using the Length node.\nThis value is used to drive an unipolar Saw Oscillator node.\nThis allows us to \"cycle\" through the string.\n\nWe've added some value to the length of the string to make it stop for a while in the end.\nThis is caused by the Saw Oscillator providing a longer length than the actual string and the Substring node not being in wrapping mode."
					}
				},
